  ```java
  if (q.length != d.length * Byte.SIZE) {
      throw new IllegalArgumentException("vector dimensions incompatible: " + q.length + "!= " + Byte.SIZE + " x " + d.length);
  }
  ```
  This check assumes that each byte in `d` corresponds to `Byte.SIZE` elements in `q`. However, the logic inside the methods suggests that each bit in `d` should correspond to one element in `q`. The correct dimension check should be:
  ```java
  if (q.length != d.length * 8) {
      throw new IllegalArgumentException("vector dimensions incompatible: " + q.length + "!= " + d.length * 8);
  }
  ```
