  ```
  The `& 0xFF` operation is unnecessary because `a[i] & b[i]` already results in a byte value, and `Integer.bitCount` correctly handles it. This can be simplified to:
  ```java
  for (; i < a.length; i++) {
      distance += Integer.bitCount(a[i] & b[i]);
  }
